=============actuator=================
http://localhost:8080/actuator/loggers/org.springframework.web

### Create a new registration

POST localhost:8080/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{"productId": 801, "attendeeName": "Jesper de Jong"}

### Get all registrations

GET localhost:8080/registrations
Accept: application/json

### Get a list of Actuator endpoints

GET localhost:8080/actuator

### Check service health

GET localhost:8080/actuator/health

### Get information about request mappings

GET localhost:8080/actuator/mappings

### Get logging level

GET localhost:8080/actuator/loggers/org.springframework.web

### Change logging level

POST localhost:8080/actuator/loggers/org.springframework.web
Content-Type: application/json

{"configuredLevel": "DEBUG"}

### Metrics overview

GET localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/http.server.requests

### Show the number of POST requests to the path /registrations

GET localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/http.server.requests?tag=method:POST&tag=uri:/registrations



=============================================================
implement actuator prometheus and grafana


   <dependency>
       <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
       <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
   </dependency>
   <dependency>
       <groupId>io.micrometer</groupId>
       <artifactId>micrometer-registry-prometheus</artifactId>
   </dependency>
==============================================
add prometheus to application.yaml

==========================================
  tickets:
    events:
      url: http://localhost:8081

  management:
    endpoints:
      web:
        exposure:
          include: health, env, beans, conditions, mappings, loggers, metrics, info, prometheus
    endpoint:
      health:
        show-details: always
      env:
        show-values: always
      prometheus:
        enabled: true
============================================

Run Your Spring Boot App
Spring Boot will expose metrics at:

http://localhost:8080/actuator/prometheus

======================================================
Configure Prometheus to Scrape Metrics .create prometheus.yaml under application.yaml
In prometheus.yml:

global:
  scrape_interval: 15s

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: 'spring-boot-app'
    metrics_path: '/actuator/prometheus'
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['host.docker.internal:8080']  # or whatever port your Spring Boot app runs on

      =====================================================

